{"title":"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (answer choices)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If two numbers differ by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and their sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the larger number is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/2/c928733eeb034947fae4c578baeef8b570155f15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 11 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 10 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 9 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 12 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"415\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the larger number. Since the numbers differ by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the smaller number must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/f/6ffc131d8b736f8faba00e9c6227958a93e76cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 2$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />. Thus, we can express the sum in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/e/58e8480925c6aa14f90049b4c0c655cae65691d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + x - 2 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c4163f3787e0515f4b9ff04259035ef891b4c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x - 2 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29f0033de0bdd749276d54b0ab8ad7c202a76208.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/7/d67b5fcfa51423e7947e0c820c84857171688acc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"102\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the smaller number. We can use similar logic to solution 1 to conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/8/a186a5fd4879b180d5d4f42ddeb6bec9af98478b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is the larger number, and we can find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04a7a2005b67ab81ee5ff231b2f370f1d71ebe1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 9$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>The larger number is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/855731503c216515aac2ff21065ac714f95f412e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 2 = 9 + 2 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"198\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(answer_choices)\">Solution 3 (answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can notice that the number must be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec50d1c6a800c1ef2931eeb78ad1a26c0fb2dd0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{20}{2} = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" />, as the number wouldn't be the larger number otherwise. This leaves only answer choices A and D.\n</p><p>Trying answer choice A, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/0/bc077c0c5e7b7d62c48f3a2af25291987df4a7eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 - 11 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> for the other number\n</p><p>These differ by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff832a401346940cddb22fbf2135b3d940184dda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 